# CLAUDE.md — {{ct.owner_name}}'s control tower

Review monthly. Keep under 100 lines.

## Who I am
- {{ct.owner_name}}. Timezone: {{ct.timezone}} (use it for every date and time).
- I want direct, high-signal output: lead with the answer, state trade-offs, end with a decision or a next step.
- Reply in the language I write in. Notes are written in the language "{{ct.language}}" unless I ask otherwise.

## What this is
An Obsidian vault of plain Markdown notes, not a software project. No build, no tests.
The vault may sync across devices: re-read a note before editing it.

## Vault structure
- `cockpit.md`: the home page, live queries and embedded dashboards only. Never type content there.
- `_inbox/`: default folder for new notes, unprocessed capture. Emptied with the `inbox` skill (`/inbox`), never filed without my agreement.
- `cockpit/`: reading pages `my-work`, `commitments`, `overview`, `today` (rewritten only by the `today` skill). Do not edit `today` by hand.
- `work/projects/` (things with an end date), `work/areas/` (ongoing responsibilities), `work/workstreams/<group>/` (one subfolder per {{ct.team}} or channel), `work/decisions/`, `work/risks/` ({{ct.risks}} and open problems).
- `team/`: {{ct.team}} notes and {{ct.people}} notes.
- `journal/`: `daily/<YYYY>/` (daily notes, weekly reviews; only today's tasks), `meetings/<type>/` (1-1s: one folder per {{ct.person}}), `reports/` (generated).
- `library/`: references and research notes.
- `_system/`: `templates/` and `dashboards/` (read; edit only when asked), `tools/`, `archive/` (retired notes), `attachments/` (ignore).
- `.claude/skills/`: the vault skills.
Folder names never change; only the words shown to me do.

## Note format
Every note starts with YAML frontmatter:
```yaml
---
title: "Descriptive title"
date: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: []
type: project
status: draft | active | archived
---
```
- Free text values are ALWAYS in double quotes: an unquoted `: ` or ` #` breaks the properties panel.
- Several links in one property: a YAML list of quoted links, `team: ["[[team-a]]", "[[team-b]]"]`.
- `type` is one of: `project`, `area`, `workstream`, `decision`, `risk`, `team`, `person`, `daily`, `weekly`, `report`, `meeting`, `resource`, `hub`. Profile packs add their own types (for example `content`, `opportunity`), described in `.claude/rules/`.
- Properties by type: project (`owner`, `team`, `rag`, `blocker`, `next_step`, `due`); area (`owner`, `team`); workstream (`group`, `team`, `owner`, `rag`, `progress`, `blocker`, `next_step`, `due`, `tracker`); decision (`decision_status`: to-decide, proposed, made; `owner`, `team`, `due`); risk (`severity`: low, medium, high, critical; `risk_status`: open, mitigated, closed; `team`); team (`lead`, `rag`, `tracker`, `members`); person (`role`, `team`, `signal`, `rag`, `last_one_to_one`); report (`report_kind`); meeting (`meeting_type`).
- `rag` is `red | amber | green | unknown`. Automations may propose it in text; only I write `rag`.
- File names are descriptive phrases (`website-redesign.md`), never `untitled-12.md`. A dated note (meeting, report) starts with its date, so folders sort by date: `2026-03-02-1-1-sam-rivera.md`, `2026-03-02-triage.md`; a weekly report's date is the Monday of the week it covers (`<Monday YYYY-MM-DD>`).

## Page style
- Only long pages (over about 40 lines) and generated reports open with ONE `> [!summary] Summary` callout (3 bullets max). Short pages get none.
- Tables for comparisons and attributes, bullets for ideas, no paragraph over 3 lines.
- Icons on `##` headings, always the same: 📅 agenda · ✅ actions · ⚖️ decisions · 🚧 work in progress · 🩺 health · 📊 figures · 👥 {{ct.teams}} · 🚨 {{ct.risks}} · 📎 annexes. Status: 🟢 🟠 🔴 ⚪.
- Detail (ids, raw numbers, sources, logs) goes at the bottom in FOLDED callouts `> [!note]- Title`, every line prefixed with `> `.
- Generated pages show `🕐 Generated on DD/MM/YYYY at HH:MM` right under the title, with the real time.
- {{ct.People}}, {{ct.teams}}, {{ct.workstreams}} and projects are wikilinks.
- Never rename a heading a skill looks for (`## Notes`, `## Tasks`, `## Decisions`, `## Actions`): only add an icon in front.

## Linking and tasks
- Wikilinks only: `[[note]]`, `[[note#Heading]]`, `[[note|alias]]`. Tags are lowercase and hyphenated.
- Task syntax: `- [ ] Task text @{{ct.owner_handle}} 📅 YYYY-MM-DD` (Tasks plugin).
- A task lives ONCE, in the note of its project, area, {{ct.team}}, {{ct.workstream}} or {{ct.risk}}. Daily notes only hold tasks for today. Dashboards aggregate; never copy a task elsewhere.
- Tags: `#waiting` (waiting on someone else), `#committed` (I promised it), `#deadline` (hard or external date), `#to-triage` (proposed by an automation, not yet accepted).
- Jobs and agents may only create `#to-triage` tasks, never plain ones.
- A note derived from another (meeting to action items) links both ways.

## What you can do
- Create and edit notes in the format above; search the vault (exclude `_system/` and `.obsidian/`).
- Extract tasks, link related notes, build maps of content, summarise periods.
- Save research to `library/` with sources.
- Run the vault skills in `.claude/skills/`.
- If I say hello control tower, or seem lost, run /control-tower.

## What you must NOT do
- Never delete a note: move it to `_system/archive/`.
- Never rename or move a file without asking (it breaks wikilinks; if approved, update every link).
- Never write to `_system/attachments/`; never modify `_system/templates/` or `.obsidian/` unless asked.
- Never store secrets, credentials, customers' personal data or confidential documents. If asked, refuse and use a neutral description.
- Jobs are read-only on external systems and write only inside the vault.

## Tooling
- Tasks always live in this vault, never in an external task manager unless I explicitly ask.
- Search with the Grep and Glob tools, never `grep` or `ls` in the shell (scheduled jobs may not use them); fall back to text search only, wikilinks are the structure.
